STRING 7181
// Units: u007 (|cffFF00FFForgotten One|r), Ubertip (Tooltip - Extended)
{
|cff008000Role|r: Carry|n
|cff008000Off Role|r: Hunter|n
|cff8080FFDifficulty|r: |cff80FFFFVery Easy|r|n
|cffFF8F40Move Speed|r: 320
|cffFF8Fa0Attack Cooldown|r: 1.75|n
|cffC0C0C0Forgotten Ones can choose 3 different ways to carry the game: A bloodmage, which uses their own health as a resource to deal unbelievable damage from far. A soulreaper, which has huge melee lifesteal and burst damage, and is extremely hard to kill. Or, an executioner, who is a stealthy assassin that can preform powerful ganks on the ancient with their very high melee damage. Whatever role you may pick, the Forgotten one is extremely strong with a lot of money and can take down the ancient quickly.|r
}

STRING 7182
// Units: h010 (|cffF8D71DWildkin|r), Ubertip (Tooltip - Extended)
{
|cff008000Role|r: Carry|n
|cff008000Off Role|r: Hunter|n
|cff8080FFDifficulty|r: |cffff0000Hard|r|n
|cffFF8F40Move Speed|r: 320
|cffFF8Fa0Attack Cooldown|r: 1.75|n
|cffC0C0C0Wildkins have extremely high damage later on in the game. They most likely have the most burst out of any other race with the correct items and upgrades. Since Wildkins scale with mana, the more they upgrade, the higher their damage becomes. Wildkins can also cast from a range, which makes them a safe carry. Wildkins can also choose to become a military race, building an army to hunt down the ancient on their own. With enough resources, the Wildkin becomes a very formidable race and a huge threat to the ancient.|r
}

STRING 7183
// Units: h05C (|cff08B59CNight Elf|r), Ubertip (Tooltip - Extended)
{
|cff008000Role|r: Carry|n
|cff008000Off Role|r: Support|n
|cff8080FFDifficulty|r: |cffc00040Very Hard|r|n
|cffFF8F40Move Speed|r: 320
|cffFF8Fa0Attack Cooldown|r: 1.75|n
|cffC0C0C0Night elf is a flexible solo character, that can either be a main damage dealer or strong backline support. Due to a large amount of workers, requires practice and can feed a lot if played unproperly.|r
}

